---
// Brand book chapters 04-05: the mark and the family it heads.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Chapter from './Chapter.astro';
import Logo from '../primitives/Logo.astro';
import markPaper from '../../../brand/logos/svg/odd-mark-paper.svg';
import markInk from '../../../brand/logos/svg/odd-mark-ink.svg';
import icon from '../../../brand/logos/svg/odd-icon.svg';
import oddfest from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddfest-paper.svg';
import oddference from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddference-paper.svg';
import oddspace from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddspace-paper.svg';
import oddstudio from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddstudio-paper.svg';
import oddagency from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddagency-paper.svg';
import oddcity from '../../../brand/logos/svg/oddcity-paper.svg';
import stage from '../../assets/oddfest-2026/blue-light-performer.jpg';

// The construction numbers, as fractions of the mark's height. Kept here in
// the same terms brand/logos/build.py uses, and drawn as guides over the real
// lockup below, so the diagram cannot drift from the artwork.
const MARK_END = 434.41 / 697.17; // the mark's right edge, as a fraction of the lockup's width
const SUFFIX_X = (434.41 + 0.2709 * 137.892) / 697.17;
const BASELINE = 0.7398;
const CAP_TOP = BASELINE - 0.484;

const family = [
  {
    logo: oddfest,
    name: 'ODDfest',
    role: 'Helsinki’s creative week of independently made events.',
    ground: 'Ink',
    accent: 'Ember, plus the Ultraviolet wash — the one page that uses it',
  },
  {
    logo: oddference,
    name: 'ODDference',
    role: 'A business conference powered by creative expertise.',
    ground: 'Ink',
    accent: 'Signal',
  },
  {
    logo: oddspace,
    name: 'ODDspace',
    role: 'A year-round workspace, studios and event space in Vallila.',
    ground: 'Paper — the whole page inverts',
    accent: 'None. The inversion is its accent.',
  },
];
const later = [
  { logo: oddstudio, name: 'ODDstudio', role: 'The recording studio inside ODDspace.' },
  {
    logo: oddagency,
    name: 'ODDagency',
    role: 'Project work with organisations, under Work with ODD.',
  },
  {
    logo: oddcity,
    name: 'ODDcity',
    role: 'Generated, not yet used — proof the system takes the next name without a redesign.',
  },
];
---

<Chapter
  id="logo"
  num="04"
  title="Logo"
  premise="Three lobes that read ODD."
  statement="The only drawn thing in the whole system."
>
  <div class="bb-prose">
    <p>
      Everything else here is type, rule and photograph. The mark is the exception: one continuous
      path, three fused lobes, no version with a strapline and no second logo. Its proportions are
      fixed at 434.41 × 137.892 (3.15:1). Scale it, place it, choose Paper or Ink artwork — that is
      the whole set of decisions.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bb-row bb-row--2">
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-stage--ink bb-logo-stage">
        <Image src={markPaper} alt="The ODD mark in Paper on an Ink ground" width={420} />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Paper artwork on Ink. The default everywhere.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-stage--paper bb-logo-stage">
        <Image src={markInk} alt="The ODD mark in Ink on a Paper ground" width={420} />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Ink artwork on Paper. ODDspace, print, light applications.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">Clear space and minimum size</h3>
  <div class="bb-row bb-row--2">
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage">
        <div
          style="outline: 1px dashed var(--color-paper-20); padding: 2rem; display: grid; place-items: center;"
        >
          <Logo class="bb-clear-mark" ariaHidden />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Clear space is half the mark’s height on every side — the dashed field. Nothing enters it:
        no type, no photograph edge, no other logo.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div
        class="bb-stage"
        style="align-content: center; justify-items: start; gap: var(--space-6);"
      >
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-4);">
          <Logo class="bb-min-mark" ariaHidden />
          <span class="t-small t-muted">Mark, minimum 12px tall (4mm in print)</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-4);">
          <Image src={oddfest} alt="" height={16} style="height: 16px; width: auto;" />
          <span class="t-small t-muted">Lockup, minimum 16px tall (6mm in print)</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        Below these sizes the lobes close up and the suffix fills in. Use the mark alone, or set the
        name in Forta.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">The lockup, constructed</h3>
  <div class="bb-prose">
    <p>
      A product lockup is the mark plus its suffix in Forta — nothing else. Four numbers, all in
      units of the mark’s height, produce every one of them, which is why a new name never needs a
      new drawing. The guides below sit on the real ODDfest artwork.
    </p>
  </div>
  <figure class="bb-figure">
    <div class="bb-stage" style="padding-block: var(--space-10);">
      <div style="position: relative; width: min(100%, 34rem); margin-inline: auto;">
        <Image
          src={oddfest}
          alt="The ODDfest lockup with its construction guides"
          width={680}
          style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;"
        />
        <span
          style={`position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:${CAP_TOP * 100}%;border-top:1px solid var(--color-signal);`}
        ></span>
        <span
          style={`position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:${BASELINE * 100}%;border-top:1px solid var(--color-signal);`}
        ></span>
        <span
          style={`position:absolute;top:-8%;bottom:-8%;left:${MARK_END * 100}%;border-left:1px solid var(--color-heat);`}
        ></span>
        <span
          style={`position:absolute;top:-8%;bottom:-8%;left:${SUFFIX_X * 100}%;border-left:1px solid var(--color-heat);`}
        ></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Blue: the suffix’s cap height and baseline. Ember: the mark’s edge and the suffix’s origin.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <dl class="bb-spec">
    <dt>Suffix cap height</dt>
    <dd>0.484 × the mark’s height</dd>
    <dt>Baseline</dt>
    <dd>0.7398 × the mark’s height, from the top</dd>
    <dt>Mark to suffix</dt>
    <dd>
      0.2709 × the mark’s height, measured origin to origin — the sidebearings do the optical work
    </dd>
    <dt>Tracking</dt>
    <dd>0.09em, with Forta’s own kerning left on</dd>
    <dt>Generated by</dt>
    <dd>
      <code>python3 brand/logos/build.py</code> — add a name to <code>LOCKUPS</code> and it exists
    </dd>
  </dl>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">Backgrounds</h3>
  <div class="bb-row">
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-stage--ink bb-logo-stage bb-logo-stage--sm">
        <Image src={markPaper} alt="" width={300} />
      </div>
      <figcaption><span class="bb-verdict">Do</span> — Paper on Ink.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-stage--paper bb-logo-stage bb-logo-stage--sm">
        <Image src={markInk} alt="" width={300} />
      </div>
      <figcaption><span class="bb-verdict">Do</span> — Ink on Paper.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-scrim" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;">
        <Image src={stage} alt="" widths={[400, 800]} sizes="30vw" />
        <div style="inset: 0; display: grid; place-items: center;">
          <Image src={markPaper} alt="" width={260} style="width: 55%; height: auto;" />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict">Do</span> — on a photograph, with the Ink scrim under it.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">Misuse</h3>
  <div class="bb-misuse">
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <Image src={markPaper} alt="" width={300} style="transform: scaleX(1.35);" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> stretch or squash it. One aspect ratio.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <Image src={markPaper} alt="" width={300} style="transform: rotate(-9deg);" />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> rotate or tilt it. The mark is always level.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <Logo class="bb-misuse-mark" ariaHidden />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> recolour it. Paper or Ink, never an accent.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <Image
          src={markPaper}
          alt=""
          width={300}
          style="filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 10px rgb(14 9 11 / 90%));"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> add shadows, outlines or effects. Use a
        scrim instead.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
          <Logo class="bb-misuse-inline" ariaHidden />
          <span style="font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.5rem;"
            >FEST</span
          >
        </span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> set the suffix in anything but Forta.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <div class="bb-misuse-stage">
        <span class="t-heading">ODD Fest · Oddfest · ODDFEST</span>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="bb-verdict bb-verdict--dont">Don’t</span> break the name. It is ODDfest: one word,
        ODD in capitals.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">The living mark, and the small mark</h3>
  <div class="bb-row bb-row--2">
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-stage--ink bb-logo-stage">
        <Logo class="bb-steam-mark" ariaHidden />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        On a hero, the mark is displaced by a turbulence filter — sauna steam, moving slowly. It is
        the one place the artwork itself is allowed to move; it holds still under reduced motion and
        never appears in print or in a deck.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="bb-figure">
      <div class="bb-stage bb-logo-stage" style="gap: var(--space-5);">
        <Image
          src={icon}
          alt="The ODD app icon: the Paper mark on an Ink tile"
          width={160}
          style="width: 8rem;"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        The app icon and favicon: the Paper mark on an Ink tile, corners at 24/128. The only place
        the mark sits inside a shape.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Chapter>

<Chapter
  id="architecture"
  num="05"
  title="Brand architecture"
  premise="One mark, one suffix."
  statement="No sub-brand ever gets a logo of its own."
>
  <div class="bb-prose">
    <p>
      ODD is the masterbrand and the only mark. A product is that mark with its name completed in
      Forta — so the family reads as one thing at a glance, and a new name costs a script run rather
      than an identity project. “All Things ODD” is the name of the house: the website, this book,
      the publisher line on a deck. It never replaces ODD in running copy.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bb-arch">
    <div class="bb-arch-top">
      <Image src={markPaper} alt="ODD" width={260} />
      <p class="t-small t-muted">
        All Things ODD — the umbrella. Operated by New Nordic Way rf, Helsinki.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bb-arch-products">
      {
        family.map((p) => (
          <div>
            <Image src={p.logo} alt={p.name} height={28} />
            <p>{p.role}</p>
            <p class="t-eyebrow">{p.ground}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div class="bb-arch-products">
      {
        later.map((p) => (
          <div class="is-future">
            <Image src={p.logo} alt={p.name} height={28} />
            <p>{p.role}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">What never changes, what a product may choose</h3>
  <div class="bb-row bb-row--2">
    <div class="bb-cell bb-cell--raised">
      <span class="bb-cell-num">Fixed</span>
      <ul class="bb-prose" style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem;">
        <li>The mark, and the four numbers that build a lockup.</li>
        <li>Forta and Gabarito, and the five-size ladder.</li>
        <li>The spacing system and the two container widths.</li>
        <li>Ink or Paper as the ground. Nothing else.</li>
        <li>Square for content, pill for what you touch.</li>
        <li>Photography as evidence: the archive, not stock.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="bb-cell">
      <span class="bb-cell-num">Free</span>
      <ul class="bb-prose" style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem;">
        <li>Which ground: Ink by default, Paper where the thing is daylight and physical.</li>
        <li>One accent, or none — Ember, Signal, or the Ultraviolet wash on ODDfest.</li>
        <li>Its hero: photo mosaic, film, or a single photograph.</li>
        <li>Its rail words: product · city · year.</li>
        <li>Its subject matter in photography.</li>
        <li>Its own copy, in the ODD voice.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">Writing the names</h3>
  <dl class="bb-spec">
    <dt>Correct</dt>
    <dd>
      ODD · ODDfest · ODDference · ODDspace · ODDstudio · ODDagency · Work with ODD · All Things ODD
    </dd>
    <dt>Never</dt>
    <dd>
      Oddfest · ODD Fest · ODDFest · odd fest · “the ODD Festival”. One word, ODD in capitals, the
      suffix lowercase.
    </dd>
    <dt>In Forta</dt>
    <dd>
      The face is unicase, so it capitalises for you. Write sentence case; never type in capitals.
    </dd>
    <dt>All Things ODD</dt>
    <dd>
      The site and publisher name — <code>og:site_name</code>, this book, the back page of a deck.
      Not a replacement for ODD in a sentence.
    </dd>
    <dt>New name</dt>
    <dd>ODD + one lowercase word, ideally under eight letters, that says what the thing is.</dd>
  </dl>

  <h3 class="bb-h3">Adding the next one</h3>
  <ol class="bb-prose" style="padding-left: 1.2rem;">
    <li>Name it: <code>ODD</code> + one lowercase word.</li>
    <li>
      Add it to <code>LOCKUPS</code> in <code>brand/logos/build.py</code> and run it. The lockup exists,
      in both colours, correct by construction.
    </li>
    <li>Choose the ground: Ink unless the thing is daylight and physical, like ODDspace.</li>
    <li>Choose at most one accent — or none.</li>
    <li>Give it rail words: the product, the city, the year.</li>
    <li>Find its photographs. If it has none yet, borrow the archive; never buy stock.</li>
    <li>Design nothing else. Everything it needs already exists.</li>
  </ol>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .bb-clear-mark {
    height: 4rem;
    width: auto;
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .bb-min-mark {
    height: 12px;
    width: auto;
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .bb-misuse-mark {
    width: 62%;
    height: auto;
    color: var(--color-amber-bright);
  }
  .bb-misuse-inline {
    height: 1.5rem;
    width: auto;
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }
  .bb-steam-mark {
    width: min(100%, 22rem);
    height: auto;
    color: var(--color-paper);
    filter: url(#steam-hero);
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .bb-steam-mark {
      filter: none;
    }
  }
</style>
